add('4:d',['A1.1.4'],'A monitoring program retains every reading in RAM. Outline why sampling every hour rather than every minute reduces its working-memory requirement, assuming equal-size records over the same day.','It stores24 readings rather than1440, so storage for the reading records is reduced by a factor of60, leaving more working memory available.',[(1,'Fewer retained reading records,24 versus1440.'),(1,'Explains proportionately lower RAM use.')],[11],status='B',adapt='Retains sampling/storage reasoning through explicit RAM working-data context,not simulation data-collection theory.')
add('4:e',['B2.2.2','B1.1.2'],'Without writing code, describe a procedure to store24 hourly readings in parallel lists hours and readings so that each time is clearly associated with its measurement.','Create two lists with24 corresponding positions. For each index0..23, store that hour in hours[index] and its measured value in readings[index]. Process all24 indices and keep the same ordering in both lists so index i links the time and reading.',[(1,'Two parallel lists/24 positions.'),(1,'Hours0..23 or equivalent clear times.'),(1,'Procedure processes every hour.'),(1,'Stores each measurement at matching index.'),(1,'Explains preserved index association.')],[11],status='B',adapt='Retains no-code parallel-list procedure and algorithmic design; no spreadsheet implementation required.')
c='''def day_stats(hours, readings):
    low = high = readings[0]
    total = night_total = 0
    night_count = 0
    for i in range(len(readings)):
        value = readings[i]
        total += value
        if value < low:
            low = value
        if value > high:
            high = value
        if hours[i] >= 19 or hours[i] < 7:
            night_total += value
            night_count += 1
    return high, low, total / len(readings), night_total / night_count'''
add('4:f',['B2.2.2','B2.3.2','B2.3.3'],'Construct day_stats(hours,readings) for24 parallel entries,one for each whole hour0..23. Return maximum,minimum,overall mean and night mean in that order. Night is hours19..23 and0..6. Use a loop to assess traversal,comparison and accumulation rather than min,max,sum or sorting.','One solution:\n'+c,[(1,'Initializes extrema from valid reading.'),(1,'Initializes totals and night count.'),(1,'Traverses all corresponding readings/hours.'),(1,'Accumulates total.'),(1,'Correct minimum update.'),(1,'Correct maximum update.'),(1,'Night condition uses >=19 OR <7 and accumulates correct subset.'),(1,'Returns extrema and correct means after traversal.')],[12],status='B',code=c,test_code=c+'\nr=day_stats(list(range(24)),list(range(24)))\nassert r[:3]==(23,0,11.5) and r[3]==10.5\nassert day_stats(list(range(24)),[-4]*24)==(-4,-4,-4.0,-4.0)',check='Executed hourly sequence/night-wrap and all-negative equal values.',source_issues=['Official MS sample night condition uses >=19 AND <7,which is impossible; adaptation correctly uses OR.'])
