add('5:c',['A4.3.3'],'Evaluate testing a trained ML flood-warning model only on examples used during training,compared with using held-out representative cases.','Training-only scores can be optimistic because the model may fit those particular examples. Held-out cases test prediction on unseen data and better reveal overfitting. They should represent relevant conditions and include difficult cases; a small or unrepresentative test set still gives uncertain evidence. Prefer a separate representative test set,review appropriate performance measures and investigate errors before deployment.',[(1,'Training-only results can be optimistic.'),(1,'Explains memorization/overfitting.'),(1,'Held-out cases test generalization.'),(1,'Representative/difficult cases improve relevance.'),(1,'Explains remaining sampling/coverage limitation.'),(1,'Supported evaluation/recommendation.')],[13],status='B',adapt='Retains validation-with-known-results reasoning through explicit ML dataset splitting/evaluation,not general simulation testing.')
