add('6:c',['A1.1.2','A1.1.4'],'Discuss processing-time and memory considerations when a live3D display adds many more objects and higher-resolution textures.','More objects/pixels increase rendering work and can reduce frame rate unless processing throughput increases. A GPU can perform many similar graphics operations in parallel. Larger textures and working results need more RAM; insufficient capacity may force extra transfers or reduced detail. Choose processing and memory together against the target frame rate and acceptable detail,cost and power use.',[(1,'More graphics work increases time/reduces frame rate.'),(1,'GPU parallel-processing benefit.'),(1,'More working textures/data require RAM.'),(1,'Develops memory-capacity/transfer consequence.'),(1,'Balanced contextual hardware recommendation.')],[14],status='B')

